---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../site.config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Disclosure — ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description={`How ${siteConfig.name} earns revenue and our commitment to editorial integrity.`}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose" style="padding-block:3rem">
      <h1>Disclosure</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: June 2, 2026</em></p>

      <p>
        Transparency matters to us. Here's how {siteConfig.name} earns revenue and how
        that does (and doesn't) affect our content.
      </p>

      <h2>How We Make Money</h2>

      <h3>Display Advertising</h3>
      <p>
        We display ads through Google AdSense (and potentially other ad networks in the
        future). We earn a small amount when visitors view or click on these ads. The
        presence of ads does not influence our editorial content.
      </p>

      <h3>Guest Posts</h3>
      <p>
        We accept paid guest contributions from qualified professionals and businesses in
        the home improvement space. All guest posts are clearly attributed to their
        authors. Guest authors may receive a dofollow link in their author bio.
      </p>
      <p>
        We maintain full editorial control over all published content. We do not guarantee
        publication, and we reject submissions that don't meet our quality standards
        regardless of payment.
      </p>

      <h2>What This Means for You</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Our editorial opinions are never for sale.</li>
        <li>We never fabricate reviews, statistics, or recommendations.</li>
        <li>Sponsored or guest content is always clearly labeled.</li>
        <li>Ad placement does not influence which topics we cover or what we recommend.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Questions?</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about our revenue model or editorial practices, email us at{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
